WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.970
Thing is the Addams Family's…pet?

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.300
Handservant?

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.430
Whatever he is, he plays a big role in Netflix's
"Wednesday."

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.170
Thing steals the scene whenever he appears.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.839
As he's portrayed by Victor Dorobantu, he
can convey emotions through just his movement.

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:17.410
You can tell when he's angry or being smug.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.420
He may be just a hand, but his physical mannerisms
make him feel like a whole person.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:27.570
Thing clearly cares about Wednesday, and his
loyalty is unshakable, even when he doesn't

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.020
agree with her actions.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.050
In the episode where Wednesday finds Thing
impaled by a knife and bleeding to death,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.160
there's a palpable tension.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.020
Thankfully Uncle Fester is able to save Thing
using his electromagnetic powers, but it's

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.090
a close call.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.750
Thing is not only Wednesday's partner in crime,
he's also the voice of reason.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.460
But only in a metaphorical sense, of course.

